        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-smooth-principal-g-bundle",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $G$ be a finite-dimensional real Lie group, $M$ a smooth manifold, and $P$\na smooth manifold. A **smooth right principal $G$-bundle** is a right principal\n$G$-bundle $\\pi:P\\to M$ in the topological sense of\n[[def-principal-g-bundle-and-associated-fiber-bundle]], with the following\nadditional smooth structure: $\\pi$ and the right $G$-action are smooth, and\nthe principal-bundle charts can be chosen as equivariant diffeomorphisms\n$\\pi^{-1}(U)\\cong U\\times G$. Thus each chart respects the projection to\n$U$ and the right action on the $G$ factor. The smoothness convention is that\nof [[def-smooth-map-between-manifolds-with-boundary]]; boundaryless manifolds\nare the default in this item.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
