          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F8",
          "source": "def-exponential-map-of-a-lie-group",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, let $G$ be a finite-dimensional real Lie group\nwith identity $e$, and write $\\mathfrak g=T_eG$. For each\n$X\\in\\mathfrak g$, the existence-and-uniqueness theorem\n[[thm-one-parameter-subgroups-are-integral-curves-of-left-invariant-fields]]\nsupplies a unique one-parameter subgroup\n$\\gamma_X:\\mathbb R\\to G$ with $\\gamma_X'(0)=X$. The **exponential map of\n$G$** is the well-defined total map",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F8",
          "source": "thm-one-parameter-subgroups-are-integral-curves-of-left-invariant-fields",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $G$ be a finite-dimensional real Lie group\nwith Lie algebra $\\mathfrak g=T_eG$.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F9",
          "source": "def-finite-dimensional-representation-of-a-group-over-a-field",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $k$ be a field ([[def-field]]) and let $G$ be a group. A\n**finite-dimensional representation of $G$ over $k$** is a finite-dimensional\n$k$-vector space $V$ ([[def-vector-space]], [[def-dimension]]) together with a\ngroup homomorphism\n$$\\rho:G\\longrightarrow \\operatorname{GL}(V),$$\nwhere $\\operatorname{GL}(V)$ denotes the group of invertible $k$-linear maps\n$V \\to V$ ([[def-linear-isomorphism-and-invertible-linear-map]], [[def-group-homomorphism]]).",
          "uses": [
