research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/preimages/research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-alpha-step1-drift.md:116:The page already declares reductive-affine-invariant-theory-and-geometric-quotients (order 0), and the imported hashes match the root carriers. The actual consumer def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient nevertheless relies on thm-complete-reducibility-and-reynolds-operator-for-complex-reductive-group and lem-reynolds-operator-and-invariant-subring-properties (each published with judge-only verification), plus thm-invariant-ring-finite-generation-and-affine-categorical-quotient (published without a verification record). I read the local proofs and the complete relevant arguments in Milne, Algebraic Groups (2022), Theorem 22.42 and Corollary 22.43 (https://www.jmilne.org/math/Books/iAG2022.pdf), and Brion, Introduction to actions of algebraic groups (2010), Theorem 1.24 (https://www.numdam.org/item/CCIRM_2010__1_1_1_0/); I found no mathematical defect, but the native proof-acceptance status remains unresolved. Owner resolution: complete the required proof review or provide an accepted local proof. Downstream affected claims include prop-aqft-integration-by-parts-eom-and-field-redefinition-redundancy and thm-aqft-field-redefinition-observable-equivalence-at-fixed-order, followed by the operator-basis, matching, SMEFT/HEFT, and amplitude consumers.
