research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/invariant-review.md:45:| `def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient` | Invariant-theory premise accepted in context. Define the finite monomial/jet space, field multiplicities, coefficient field, dimensions, derivative cutoff, symmetry action and relation subspace. Prove the action is rational and relations stable. For a rational module `V` and stable subspace `N`, Reynolds exactness gives `(V/N)^G = V^G/(N intersect V^G)` canonically. State the map and verify its kernel and surjectivity; this is the correct linear quotient interface. Ring-ideal conclusions require an actual ideal. |
