research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/invariant-review.md-52-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/invariant-review.md-53-For fermions, a supercommutative Grassmann algebra is not the commutative reduced affine coordinate algebra assumed by the finite-generation/affine-quotient theorem. The rational-module projection and exactness statements can apply to its finite-dimensional underlying representation, once that action is specified, without pretending it is a reduced affine variety. Fixed engineering dimension is finite only after finite generators/jet order and suitable positive weights or another explicit finiteness restriction are given. Neither finite generation nor averaging supplies Hilbert-series enumeration, all local gauge invariants or any infinite completion for free.
