research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/invariant-review.md:57:The smallest unresolved issue in the drift finding is proof-status reconciliation, not a missing invariant-theory theorem. This fresh mathematical reading supports resolving that planning hold with root-owned evidence. The three original publication audit omissions remain exactly as observed: judge-only on the bridge and Reynolds lemma; no verification stamp on the quotient theorem. Additional transitive omissions are not repaired by this report. No duplicate theorem or new support pair is warranted merely to manufacture stamps.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/invariant-review.md-58-
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/invariant-review.md-59-The smallest substantive *consumer* work remains the already assigned finite operator quotient construction with a stable relation subspace and its fixed-order variational/observable proof. These are existing authoring obligations, not proved by this review, not new open problems, and not grounds to claim readiness or omit substantial approved EFT scope. If authoring later exposes an actual additional prerequisite, record its exact interface and consumers before adding a genuinely needed support pair. Root alone owns receipt integration, current-input hashes, the hold decision and native gates.
