research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/preimages/research/plan-spec.json:41518:          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Let $H$ be a nonzero complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]) and $(F_1,\\dots,F_n)$ a finite POVM on $H$: a finite family of bounded self-adjoint operators $0\\le F_a\\le I$ with $\\sum_aF_a=I$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-finite-effects-and-instruments]]). Let $C=\\mathbb C^n$ with standard orthonormal basis $(e_a)$ and form $H\\widehat\\otimes C$ ([[lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction]]). Then\n\n$$W:H\\to H\\widehat\\otimes C,\\qquad W\\psi:=\\sum_{a=1}^nF_a^{1/2}\\psi\\otimes e_a,$$\n\nis a linear isometry, the operators $P_a:=I_H\\otimes T_{e_a,e_a}$ are orthogonal projections with $\\sum_aP_a=I$ (a finite PVM on $\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$, [[def-hilbert-orthogonal-projection]]), and\n\n$$W^*P_aW=F_a\\qquad(a=1,\\dots,n).$$\n\nThe square roots $F_a^{1/2}$ are the positive square roots supplied by the bounded functional calculus. The construction asserts no physical realization of the ancilla.",
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/preimages/research/plan-spec.json-41519-          "strategy": "Take bounded positive square roots by the continuous functional calculus, compute \u2016W\u03c8\u2016\u00b2=\u03a3_a\u27e8F_a\u03c8,\u03c8\u27e9=\u2016\u03c8\u2016\u00b2, and identify the compressions W*P_aW by matrix elements in the ancilla basis.",
