research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/preimages/research/plan-spec.json:41786:          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice and the Axiom of Choice ([[def-countable-choice]], [[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Fix $m>0$, $\\hbar>0$, $\\sigma>0$ and real $x_0,p_0$, and let\n\n$$\\psi_0(x):=(2\\pi\\sigma^2)^{-1/4}\\exp\\Bigl(-\\frac{(x-x_0)^2}{4\\sigma^2}\\Bigr)\\exp\\Bigl(i\\frac{p_0(x-x_0)}{\\hbar}\\Bigr),\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb R .$$\n\nLet $H_0$ be the free operator of clause (b) of [[thm-nrqm-composites-real-multipliers-and-free-bounded-potential-operators]] with $c:=2\\pi^2\\hbar^2/m$ and $b:=0$, i.e.\n\n$$H_0:=\\mathcal F_2^*\\,M_{2\\pi^2\\hbar^2\\xi^2/m}\\,\\mathcal F_2,\\qquad D(H_0)=\\{f\\in L^2(\\mathbb R):\\xi^2\\mathcal F_2f\\in L^2(\\mathbb R)\\},$$\n\nwhich is self-adjoint with $D(H_0)=W^{2,2}(\\mathbb R;\\mathbb C)$ and $H_0f=-\\frac{\\hbar^2}{2m}\\Delta f$ for $f\\in\\mathcal S(\\mathbb R)$. Let $U$ be the momentum transform of [[lem-nrqm-composites-momentum-fourier-jacobian]], the surjective isometry $L^2(\\mathbb R,dx)\\to L^2(\\mathbb R,dp)$ with $U=D_\\hbar\\circ\\mathcal F_2$ on $\\mathcal S(\\mathbb R)$. For $t\\in\\mathbb R$ put $\\tau:=\\frac{\\hbar t}{2m\\sigma^2}$ and\n\n$$\\psi_t(x):=(2\\pi\\sigma^2)^{-1/4}(1+i\\tau)^{-1/2}\\exp\\Bigl(-\\frac{(x-x_0-p_0t/m)^2}{4\\sigma^2(1+i\\tau)}+i\\frac{p_0(x-x_0)}{\\hbar}-i\\frac{p_0^2t}{2m\\hbar}\\Bigr),$$\n\nwhere $z^{-1/2}:=\\exp\\bigl(-\\tfrac12\\operatorname{Log}z\\bigr)$ is the principal branch of [[def-complex-logarithms-principal-logarithm-and-complex-powers]], legitimate at $z=1+i\\tau$ because $\\operatorname{Re}(1+i\\tau)=1>0$. Let $Qf(x)=xf(x)$ and $Pf(x)=-i\\hbar f'(x)$ act on $\\mathcal S(\\mathbb R)$. Then:\n\n(a) $\\psi_0\\in\\mathcal S(\\mathbb R)$, $\\|\\psi_0\\|_2=1$, and for every $t$ one has $\\psi_t\\in\\mathcal S(\\mathbb R)\\subseteq D(H_0)$; the map $t\\mapsto\\psi_t$ is continuously differentiable $\\mathbb R\\to L^2(\\mathbb R)$ with $\\psi_t\\in D(H_0)$ and $\\frac{d}{dt}\\psi_t=-\\frac{i}{\\hbar}H_0\\psi_t$, and consequently $\\psi_t=e^{-itH_0/\\hbar}\\psi_0$, where $e^{-itH_0/\\hbar}:=e^{itT}$ with $T:=-H_0/\\hbar$ denotes the unitary group generated by the self-adjoint operator $T$ ([[lem-self-adjoint-operator-generates-a-strongly-continuous-unitary-group]]).\n\n(b) _Position density._ $|\\psi_t(x)|^2=\\bigl(2\\pi\\sigma^2(1+\\tau^2)\\bigr)^{-1/2}\\exp\\bigl(-(x-x_0-p_0t/m)^2/(2\\sigma^2(1+\\tau^2))\\bigr)$; it is a probability density of mean $x_0+p_0t/m$ and variance $\\sigma^2(1+\\tau^2)$.\n\n(c) _Momentum density._ $|U\\psi_t(p)|^2=\\sqrt{2/\\pi}\\,(\\sigma/\\hbar)\\exp\\bigl(-2\\sigma^2(p-p_0)^2/\\hbar^2\\bigr)=|U\\psi_0(p)|^2$ for almost every $p$; it is a probability density of mean $p_0$ and variance $\\hbar^2/(4\\sigma^2)$, independent of $t$.\n\n(d) _Standard deviations._ With $\\Delta Q:=\\|(Q-\\langle Q\\psi_t,\\psi_t\\rangle)\\psi_t\\|_2$ and $\\Delta P:=\\|(P-\\langle P\\psi_t,\\psi_t\\rangle)\\psi_t\\|_2$ one has $\\Delta Q=\\sigma\\sqrt{1+\\tau^2}$, $\\Delta P=\\hbar/(2\\sigma)$ and\n\n$$\\Delta Q\\,\\Delta P=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\sqrt{1+\\tau^2}\\ \\ge\\ \\frac{\\hbar}{2},$$\n\nwith equality exactly at $t=0$; the lower bound $\\hbar/2$ is the one supplied by clause (d) of [[lem-nrqm-composites-weak-form-robertson-uncertainty]] with $c=\\hbar$.\n\n(e) _Scope._ These are exact conditional calculations for the free model defined by $H_0$; no measurement, instrument or laboratory preparation is described, and nothing here asserts that a physical wave packet is Gaussian.",
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/preimages/research/plan-spec.json-41787-          "strategy": "Transform the initial Gaussian explicitly, multiply the momentum wavefunction by e^{\u2212itp\u00b2/(2m\u210f)}, complete the square with a parameter of positive real part so the continued Gaussian identity applies, and read the moments off the resulting Gaussian densities; the uncertainty clause uses the Robertson bound with the exact variances.",
